Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Scaling Up: A GPT-2 Discussion Model", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"dfeb9171-a06d-4050-a294-0027267bc8c2"],

Cell["From the 20-pair toy SFT to a model that actually chats", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"7df988a9-873e-461e-86a3-67736e03b8db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The master notebook ended with a 124M-parameter GPT-2 model SFT'd on ",
 "20 hand-written Q&A pairs.  It learned the chat ",
 StyleBox["template",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " but its factual answers were obviously wrong (\"Hamlet is a ",
 "playwright who wrote the play in 1763\").  In this notebook we keep ",
 "the same architecture and the same training loop -- and just give ",
 "the model real data: 10,000 instruction\[Dash]response pairs from the ",
 "Apache-2.0 Alpaca-cleaned corpus (Stanford 2023).  Three SFT epochs ",
 "take 3-4 hours on a Mac mini CPU.  The result is a small but ",
 "genuinely conversational model."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cf2b1bd-1b09-419e-8e4c-5cdcd7b8bdb4"],

Cell["Two design choices worth flagging:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bc8fb34e-3684-47f3-9fae-fc38cde961b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. ",
 StyleBox["GPT-2 small (124M), not medium (345M)",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".  Medium gives a more capable base, but in our Mac-mini setup it ",
 "hits an MXNet operator-shape bug when we strip the inference tail ",
 "and re-chain for training, and per-example wall time would put any ",
 "meaningful training run beyond 8 days.  Cloud compute fixes both ",
 "issues; for the educational story we keep small and treat ",
 "RemoteBatchSubmit as the scaling switch.\n",
 "2. ",
 StyleBox["Plain-text chat template, no new vocabulary tokens",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".  The master notebook taught the canonical ",
 StyleBox["<|user|>...<|assistant|>...<|eot|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " trick.  Here we use plain ",
 StyleBox["\"User: ...\\nAssistant: ...\\n\"",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  GPT-2's BPE tokeniser already represents \"User\", \"Assistant\", ",
 "the colon, the newline; we keep the 50,257-entry vocabulary and ",
 "the weight tying intact.  Less elegant theoretically; more robust ",
 "practically."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b5bc1457-4923-4d9c-8da5-ca0bdd008553"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1.  Setup", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"1b675355-7a44-4889-bc77-dc123ca4d63f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[83]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ff311b9e-31de-42d4-b3d1-e047ca12a903"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"/Users/thiel/GitHub/LLM-A-to-Z-in-WL/discussion-model\"\>"],\
 "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988366851501524*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[83]=",ExpressionUUID->"9d0037a3-6dd0-4778-ab81-8d3ab54ab5ef"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Get[\"src/Discussion.wl\"]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[84]:=",ExpressionUUID->"300ab9ff-b14f-41db-a004-112f6195f476"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.  Load GPT-2 small and inspect", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"5767c193-6d02-43f8-b642-3a64558f80f3"],

Cell["\<\
WL ships GPT-2 in three sizes (117M, 345M, 774M) via the Neural Net \
Repository.  Loading downloads ~498 MB on first call and caches the weights \
on disk.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a983779c-5610-42d4-9b3d-fd6f67ac8800"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
gpt = LLMAtoZ`Discussion`loadGpt2Small[];
Information[gpt, \"ArraysTotalElementCount\"]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[85]:=",ExpressionUUID->"45488597-c03f-49ad-9a9e-38ebf1196cc4"],

Cell[BoxData["124439808"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9883668515775337`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[86]=",ExpressionUUID->"eb2d39e7-4870-49b4-b9dc-577030fc777d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["The pretrained net has five top-level layers:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"22ad1d51-b52f-4d63-89a6-c39204506491"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Keys @ NetExtract[gpt, All]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[87]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3db38c8e-29e1-4f78-b320-f39d497d909d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"embedding\"\>", ",", "\<\"decoder\"\>", ",", "\<\"last\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"classifier\"\>", ",", "\<\"probabilities\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",\

 CellChangeTimes->{3.9883668515807123`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[87]=",ExpressionUUID->"03cf69dc-26d3-4b98-9a78-21f2bbe7bc17"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["The structure is:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"090c7d36-c8c4-4350-9121-7f80d091e9d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["embedding",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (token + positional) \[RightArrow] ",
 StyleBox["decoder",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (12 transformer blocks for small) \[RightArrow] ",
 StyleBox["last",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (SequenceLastLayer: takes only the last position) \[RightArrow] ",
 StyleBox["classifier",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (LinearLayer: 768 \[Rule] 50,257) \[RightArrow] ",
 StyleBox["probabilities",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (SoftmaxLayer).  This wiring is for ",
 StyleBox["inference",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": one prompt in, one next-token distribution out."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46a57518-f161-4176-bbb3-6a87b488e2db"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3.  Surgery: from inference net to training trunk", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"295a91ca-9b90-4391-bc64-d0bfe246f2d0"],

Cell["\<\
For SFT we need per-position logits at every step.  Three changes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae4c75db-a411-4638-b784-801060510b96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. Drop ",
 StyleBox["SequenceLastLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " so we keep all positions of the (seqLen, dModel) decoder output.\n",
 "2. Wrap the ",
 StyleBox["classifier",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["NetMapOperator",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " so it applies row-wise rather than once.\n",
 "3. Drop the final ",
 StyleBox["SoftmaxLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " -- the training loop adds its own softmax via ",
 StyleBox["NetMapOperator[SoftmaxLayer[]]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " so that ",
 StyleBox["CrossEntropyLossLayer[\"Index\"]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " sees probabilities (the bug from Section 5.3 of the master)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57a31bd7-37a3-4ce3-b2c9-ad56246ab0f1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
trunk = LLMAtoZ`Discussion`buildTrainableTrunk[gpt];
Information[trunk, \"ArraysTotalElementCount\"]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[88]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d2df4391-2825-4c2e-96db-de5cd233af5a"],

Cell[BoxData["124439808"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988366851883337*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[89]=",ExpressionUUID->"f3e24c8a-636f-43d5-90f4-b1364037b8fd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Same parameter count as the original (we just rearranged), and the \
embedding-classifier weight tying is preserved through the bundled \
SharedArrays.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f450775-e6e1-4029-8374-332e7c18da08"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(* Sanity: feed a 4-token sequence and verify shape *)
encoder = NetExtract[gpt, \"Input\"];
ids = encoder[\"Hello world. How are you today?\"];
Print[\"ids: \", ids];
out = trunk[ids];
Print[\"output dims: \", Dimensions[out]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[90]:=",ExpressionUUID->"17be58c4-6c80-4634-b7ae-0012f9b868f0"],

