Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.  Limits and where to go", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"9763cadb-d1b5-431c-be6f-1f75a92cf2b2"],

Cell["\<\
This 124M model SFT'd for 3 epochs holds the chat format and gives plausible \
responses to general questions.  It will not pass a Turing test, and its \
factual accuracy is only as good as Alpaca's: many details are wrong.  The \
next levers, in order of impact per hour:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"253442f4-8a76-4c35-9d37-8d2ea19a411b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. ",
 StyleBox["More data + a chattier dataset.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " SmolTalk (HuggingFace, ~150k multi-turn dialogues) is a much better ",
 "fit for chat than Alpaca's single-turn instructions.\n",
 "2. ",
 StyleBox["Bigger base via cloud.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " GPT-2 medium (345M) or large (774M) SFT'd via RemoteBatchSubmit on ",
 "the same data; budget ~\[Sterling]30-100.\n",
 "3. ",
 StyleBox["RL post-training.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Apply the GRPO step from Chapter 8 of the master with a quality ",
 "reward (e.g., a small judge model that scores helpfulness).\n",
 "4. ",
 StyleBox["Modern instruct base.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " For a model that genuinely chats, the only fast path is pulling a ",
 "post-2024 instruction-tuned model (SmolLM2-360M-Instruct, Qwen2.5-",
 "0.5B-Instruct) via ONNX.  Tradeoff: breaks the from-scratch story."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7204ee74-545d-4535-bc9b-4a0c34dab18f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["References", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"d37cfbe9-2c3e-46ac-8f48-c9d5dd3c5c7e"],

